{"skill":{"slug":"memos","displayName":"Memos"},"version":{"version":"0.1.1","createdAt":1771792388319,"changelog":"- Clarified configuration requirements: both `MEMOS_URL` and `MEMOS_TOKEN` are now explicitly marked as **REQUIRED** environment variables.\n- Improved documentation to state that the skill will abort if either variable is missing.\n- Minor wording and formatting adjustments for clearer instruction and emphasis on required setup.","changelogSource":"auto","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":4107,"sha256":"aa8462e1ba494843df2755646682236e35b1fb5dbc32d18f347ded5fff9d5f45","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"memos.py","size":9658,"sha256":"ed13a87fda2bc6a3343cb28f9820d16a7a568df4ce64fda62e5189e02beb784d","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2084,"sha256":"880d592d6f4adad93200e59d5eda4efd9a715b4b2d79e47da3c2d03b49ad9c13","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789079225420,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"5ca14cf064da3af4daae23cc1a149f6610004bc1a6cc28b55398d2fe1e9a420a","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/5ca14cf064da3af4daae23cc1a149f6610004bc1a6cc28b55398d2fe1e9a420a","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: memos\nVersion: 0.1.1\n\nThe OpenClaw Memos skill is a straightforward Python client for the Memos API. It correctly uses environment variables (`MEMOS_URL`, `MEMOS_TOKEN`) for configuration and authentication, aborting if they are not set. The `SKILL.md` documentation clearly outlines its purpose and commands without any prompt injection attempts or instructions for the agent to perform unauthorized actions. The `memos.py` code implements standard API interactions with robust error handling, input validation for parameters like `visibility` and `pageSize`, and no evidence of data exfiltration, backdoors, or arbitrary code execution. All network calls are directed to the `MEMOS_URL` provided in the environment, which is a standard and expected behavior for an API integration skill.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779166305954},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":44,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":5,"checkedAt":1789079225420},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"The skill is a straightforward Memos API helper, with expected token use and memo mutation features that users should handle carefully.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The skill requires MEMOS_URL and MEMOS_TOKEN and sends the bearer token to the configured API base URL, which is expected for this integration but should be limited to a trusted HTTPS Memos instance.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"No install hooks, background setup, package-install scripts, or hidden execution mechanisms were found in the artifact; it is a Python script using requests.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The documented commands are user-directed and limited to Memos operations; delete and force-delete are disclosed but lack a prominent irreversible-deletion warning or confirmation step.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"There is no local persistence, privilege escalation, or system modification; remote memo creation and deletion persist changes in the user's Memos account as part of the stated purpose.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is to create, read, delete, and list Memos entries, and the Python implementation performs those matching API operations.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install only if you trust the Memos instance configured in MEMOS_URL, preferably over HTTPS, and use a narrowly scoped MEMOS_TOKEN. Review visibility before creating memos because PUBLIC is the default, and invoke delete or force-delete only when you are certain the remote memo should be removed.","findings":"[PE3] expected: The personal access token is explicitly required for Memos API authentication and is read from an environment variable; I found no local credential-file access or unrelated token collection.\n[P9] expected: The long spaces are Markdown table alignment in SKILL.md; inspection found no hidden instructions or concealed payload after the whitespace.\n[SQP-2] expected: The delete command is purpose-aligned and documented, but the documentation should better warn that deletion or force deletion may be irreversible.\n[SQP-2] expected: The code performs a direct DELETE request with optional force when the user invokes delete; this matches the command but has no confirmation prompt.\n[SDI-4] expected: The create function appends a newline plus #openclaw to submitted content, matching the general documented behavior though the wording overstates semantic tag guarantees.\n[T09] expected: Sending the bearer token to MEMOS_URL is expected for API authentication, but the code does not enforce HTTPS or validate the configured host, so users must avoid untrusted or plaintext endpoints.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789079225420}}}}}